course: dictionary
lesson: 1654
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «The coins chinked in his pocket.» Coins make a sound, so chinked means made a light ringing noise, not made a crack.
explain: «Toad sobs that he will go out into the dark night ... then hears the chink of dishes» Here chink is a light clinking sound, the kind dishes make when they knock together. The sound is the clue.
explain: «A chink of coin passing from paw to paw» also means a small, clinking sound of money. Ask: what would fit here? A sound. A crack in a wall would not make sense with coins passing from paw to paw.
explain: Some meanings only make sense in a set phrase. «A chink in someone's armour» means a weak spot, a place where someone can be hurt. You cannot guess this from the single words, so learn the phrase as a whole.
fact: A chink can be a narrow crack or opening, such as «light shining through a chink in the curtains».
fact: A chink can also be a light ringing sound, like coins or glasses knocking together.
fact: As a verb, «chink» means to make that sound: «The coins chinked in his pocket.»
fact: «A chink in someone's armour» means a weak spot.
fact: One meaning is a very offensive, racist insult against Chinese and East Asian people. Never use it. If you hear it, tell a teacher.
exercise: «Light came through a chink in the curtains.» What is a chink here? | A cup of tea | A loud bang | A large window | *A narrow crack or opening
exercise: «The coins chinked in his pocket.» What does chinked mean? | To fall asleep | *To make a light ringing sound | To shine brightly | To hide
exercise: «Her plan had one chink in its armour: nobody had checked the bridge.» What does chink in its armour mean? | *A weak spot | A rude remark | A very high wall | A shiny piece of metal
test: «Toad hears the chink of dishes and cries, "Supper's here at last!"» In this sentence, chink means: | A hole in the wall | A long walk | A kind of soup | *A light clinking sound
test: What part of speech is chinked in «The coins chinked in his pocket»? | Adverb | Noun | Adjective | *Verb
exam: Which meaning of chink fits «a chink of light under the door»? | A ringing bell | *A narrow crack or opening | A rude word | A large coin
